>> title: Rogan Josh
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: lamb, kashmiri, yogurt, chiles, curry
>> counters: Curry House, One Pot
>> aka: roghan josh, rogan gosht, lamb rogan josh, kashmiri lamb curry
>> pairs-with: pilau-rice, chapati, raita
>> servings: 6
>> time: 2 hr 30 min

>> step: sear 10 min in batches, until browned all over
Sear @lamb shoulder{2 1/2%lb}(1.1 kg; cut in 2-in pieces, bone in if you can get it) in @ghee{3%Tbs}(42 g) and @mustard oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL; heated to smoking first, then cooled) in a #heavy pot{} ~sear{10%min}, in two batches so the pieces brown rather than steam.

>> step: fry 1 min, until the cardamom swells
Fry @black cardamom{2%pods}(cracked), @green cardamom{4%pods}, @cloves{4}, @bay leaf{1} and @cinnamon{1%stick}(2-in piece) in @&(~1)seared lamb{} ~fry{1%min}.

>> step: stir in the slaked chile, off the heat
Stir @Kashmiri chile powder{2%Tbs} slaked in @water{1/4%cup}(60 mL) into @&(~1)lamb and whole spice{} off the heat.

>> step: whisk in a spoonful at a time, 5 min
Whisk @thick yogurt{1%cup}(240 g; whisked smooth) into @&(~1)pot{} a spoonful at a time over low heat ~stir{5%min}, waiting for each to be taken up before the next goes in, so it never breaks.

>> step: braise 1 hr 30 min, covered, until it gives to a spoon
Braise @&(~1)lamb{} with @ground fennel{1%Tbs}, @ground dried ginger{2%tsp}, @asafoetida{1/4%tsp}, @kosher salt{2%tsp} and @water{1%cup}(240 mL) covered ~simmer{90%min}, until the meat gives to the side of a spoon and the fat has come up red on top.

No onion and no tomato in this. Fennel dried ginger and asafoetida do the work instead.
